  "steps": [
   {
    "text": "In a small saucepan over medium heat, combine minced garlic cloves, soy sauce, zero-calorie brown sugar, mirin, and (optional) minced ginger. Simmer for 3–4 minutes. In a separate bowl, whisk cornstarch with cold water to create a slurry. Slowly stir slurry into the sauce. Cook until thickened. Set aside."
   },
   {
    "text": "In a bowl, combine chicken thighs with teriyaki sauce, fish sauce, and avocado oil. Mix well and marinate for at least 1 hour or overnight."
   },
   {
    "text": "Heat a skillet over high heat. Cook chicken until browned on both sides and fully cooked through. Glaze with extra teriyaki sauce in the final minute. Set aside to rest, then slice."
   },
   {
    "text": "Cook dry white rice according to package instructions."
   },
   {
    "text": "In the skillet the chicken was cooked in, add frozen vegetables and cook until tender. Push veggies to the side and crack in eggs and pour in egg whites. Scramble and cook until set. Add cooked rice and mix everything together. Drizzle with sesame oil and soy sauce. Stir well to combine and heat through."
   },
   {
    "text": "Top the fried rice with sliced teriyaki chicken. Divide into 5 servings and enjoy!"
   }
  ]
